 George [D-NY-16]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2025-02-12","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"NY"}],"fetchedAt":"2026-09-17T15:49:50+00:00","id":"hres66-119","introducedDate":"2025-01-24","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-01-24","text":"Referred to the House Committee on Foreign Affairs."},"laws":[],"number":"66","originChamber":"House","policyArea":"International Affairs","sponsors":[{"bioguideId":"M001188","district":6,"fullName":"Rep. Meng, Grace [D-NY-6]","party":"D","state":"NY"}],"summaries":[{"actionDate":"2025-01-24","actionDesc":"Introduced in House","text":"<p>This resolution commends the role of the U.S. government in improving access to quality, inclusive education, and improved learning outcomes for the poorest and most marginalized children and adolescents around the world. The resolution calls on the Department of State and the U.S. Agency for International Development to use all diplomatic, humanitarian, and developmental means to promote access to such quality education.</p>","updateDate":"2025-03-04T16:54:34Z","versionCode":"00"}],"title":"Affirming the role of the United States in improving access to quality, inclusive public education and improving learning outcomes for children and adolescents, particularly for girls, around the world.","type":"hres","updateDate":"2025-03-04T16:58:59Z","updateDateIncludingText":"2025-03-04T16:58:59Z"}
